            <ArticleTitle>Hemiarthroplasty for glenohumeral arthritis with massive rotator cuff tears.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>477-89</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rotator cuff deficiency with associated glenohumeral arthritis poses a formidable clinical challenge. Humeral head replacement with maintenance of the coracoacromial arch is the current treatment of choice. Properly performed arthroplasty can provide pain relief and modest gains in motion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
